#+TITLE: Sample notes
// The notes Settings shows its looks on (workbench/look_preview.odin): one of everything a look colours.
// Edit freely - nothing reads it but the Settings preview, and a test that it parses clean.

* Openings

A sample of the notes' look: *bold*, /italic/, _underline_ and =4NT= in the text, a [link to the
competitive section](#Competition), and the suits !c !d !h !s.

** One notrump

1N = 15--17 balanced
    2C = Stayman
        2D = no four-card major
        2H = 4+ !hs, may hold four !ss
            2N = invitational, four !ss
            3N = to play
    2D = transfer to !hs
    2H = transfer to !ss

*** Weak twos

2H = 5+ (NV) / 6+ (VUL) card weak two, 1st/2nd
    2N = ask, natural invite by a passed hand

**** The fine print

- Stayman :: 2C asks for a major
- Jacoby :: 2D and 2H transfer

* Competition

(1H)--X
    1S = 4+ !ss, 0--8
    2H = cue bid, game force

| Points | Action |
|---+---|
| 0--7 | pass |
| 8--10 | invite |
| 11+ | game |

